      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_40be4244",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: dat ass ahmarbkrich d; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The meme juxtaposes an image of sheep with their rear ends prominently displayed against a man in a headscarf and sunglasses who is screaming in apparent shock or disgust. The text 'dat ass' is overlaid on the sheep image, while 'ahmarbkrich d' (a distorted, likely misspelled or coded term) is overlaid on the man. The visual and textual elements together create a crude, mocking comparison, likely targeting individuals of Middle Eastern or Muslim appearance. This is a clear example of Islamophobia, as it uses a degrading visual metaphor (sheep butts) to mock a person's appearance and religious identity, fitting the category of hateful content. The meme relies on the stereotype of 'backward culture' and 'animal treatment' accusations, and it is designed to provoke negative reactions toward the targeted group. The intent is to demean and insult based on protected characteristics (religion/ethnicity), making it hateful and potentially harmful.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_6be1d82c"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
